      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"gentle parenting\" movement is a broad, often poorly defined trend that has been heavily criticized by child development experts. The reality is that consistent, firm boundaries and clear expectations are crucial for building discipline, not the constant permissiveness sometimes associated with this label. True resilience comes from learning to navigate limits and consequences, which requires authoritative parenting, not permissive indulgence.",
